    "modified_rtl": "  always @(posedge clk_i)\n    if(spe & (|clkcnt & |state))\n      clkcnt <= clkcnt - 11'h1;\n    else\n      case (espr) // synopsys full_case parallel_case\n        4'b0000: clkcnt <= 12'h0;   // 2   -- original M68HC11 coding\n        4'b0001: clkcnt <= 12'h1;   // 4   -- original M68HC11 coding\n        4'b0010: clkcnt <= 12'h3;   // 16  -- original M68HC11 coding\n        4'b0011: clkcnt <= 12'hf;   // 32  -- original M68HC11 coding\n        4'b0100: clkcnt <= 12'h1f;  // 8\n        4'b0101: clkcnt <= 12'h7;   // 64\n        4'b0110: clkcnt <= 12'h3f;  // 128\n        4'b0111: clkcnt <= 12'h7f;  // 256\n        4'b1000: clkcnt <= 12'hff;  // 512\n        4'b1001: clkcnt <= 12'h1ff; // 1024\n        4'b1010: clkcnt <= 12'h3ff; // 2048\n        4'b1011: clkcnt <= 12'h7ff; // 4096\n        default : clkcnt <= 12'hfff;\n      endcase",
    "rationale": "The path start and end flops both map to line 240, the only register there being clkcnt, so the violating path is the clkcnt down-counter self-loop: clkcnt bits through the 12-bit `clkcnt - 11'h1` ripple-borrow decrementer (AOI21/INV chain + XOR2 sum bit, cells 1-16), then the reload mux `spe & (|clkcnt & |state) ? (clkcnt-1) : espr_case` (final OAI22, cell 18). The middle AND/NOR/OAI cluster is the |clkcnt / |state reductions feeding that mux select. This logic is present in the shown scope.\n\nRETIME chosen as the reported strategy only in the sense that no latency may be added; in practice no move is possible: the chain is a bare DFF->comb->DFF feedback arc with no register inside it, and a single-register combinational cycle cannot be shortened by retiming (the loop delay/register-count bound is invariant). Moving clkcnt across the decrementer merely relocates the same `-1` within the same loop.\n\nPIPELINE rejected: adding a register in this arc inserts a bubble into a reload down-counter that acts as the sck clock divider, changing the SPI bit cadence (the result itself, not just its timing). Every reconvergent consumer \u2014 the `state` FSM advance and the `sck` toggle logic, both outside lines 240-258 \u2014 would need the identical extra cycle, which cannot be done within this scope and would require full-chip context I was told not to assume.\n\nNo cut or move was made and nothing was delayed: the scope is returned byte-for-byte identical to preserve equivalence. A correct fix requires restructuring outside this range (e.g. cascaded low/high sub-counters to break the borrow ripple, with matching delay on the state/sck logic)."
  },
